    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d840">

                <pb facs="0936" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Department of the Army Files: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 840<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Military Representation
                        on the Allied Control Commission for Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schuyler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the War Department</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract<anchor n="1" xml:id="d840-f1"/>]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-24">24 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>M 1285. …</p>
                <p>1. Under Article 7<anchor n="2" xml:id="d840-f2"/> the ACC has required the delivery to Russia as “War Booty” of considerable quantities of industrial equipment
                    including oil pipe, tubing and casing, on the ground that such equipment
                    originated in Germany. I propose to protest that [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >the</hi>] application of this policy to any industrial equipment,
                    regardless of its <pb facs="0937" n="743" xml:id="pg743"/> origin, which can be
                    shown to have been actually purchased and paid for prior to 23 August
                        1944.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d840-f3"/> I am informed that a similar protest
                    has been made to the Soviet Government by the US Ambassador in Moscow.<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d840-f4"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d840-f1" n="1" xml:id="d840-f1-content">
                <p>For the full text of this message, see <ref target="#d812">document No.
                    812</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d840-f2" n="2" xml:id="d840-f2-content">
                <p>Of the armistice with Rumania signed at Moscow, September 12, 1944 (Executive
                    Agreement Series No. 490; 59 Stat. (2)
                    1712).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d840-f3" n="3" xml:id="d840-f3-content">
                <p>i. e., before the surrender of Rumania.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d840-f4" n="4" xml:id="d840-f4-content">
                <p>W. Averell Harriman. See <ref
                        target="frus1945Berlinv01#d323">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>,
                        document No. 323</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
